      "sec": "TERMS tab",
      "src": 101,
      "url": "https://www.1enrollment.com/information/product.cfm?page=25653&id=974021",
      "v": "1. Treatment, services or supplies that are not medically necessary, not prescribed by a doctor as necessary to treat an injury, determined experimental or investigational, received without charge or legal obligation to pay, received from persons employed or retained by any family member, or not specifically listed as Covered Charges. 2. Injury by acts of war, declared or not. 3. Injury while travelling or flying by air except as a fare-paying passenger and not as pilot or crew on a regularly scheduled commercial airline. 4. Injury paid by Worker's Compensation, Employer Liability law or Occupational Disease Act or Law. 5. Dental treatment except as specifically stated. 6. Injury while committing or attempting to commit a felony. 7. Prescription drugs except as specifically stated. 8. Suicide or attempted suicide while sane or insane. 9. Intentionally self-inflicted injury. 10. Loss from being legally intoxicated or under the influence of alcohol as defined by the state or jurisdiction where the injury occurs. 11. Loss from being under the influence of drugs or narcotics unless administered on a doctor's advice. 12. Injury while on active duty service in any armed forces; reserve or National Guard active duty for training is not excluded unless it extends beyond 31 days. 13. Injury flying in an ultralight, hang gliding, parachuting or bungee-cord jumping, or by flight in a spacecraft or craft designed for navigation above the earth's atmosphere. 14. Injury while driving or riding on vehicles for off-road use including all terrain vehicles. 15. Injury where the insured is the operator and does not possess a current and valid motor vehicle operator's licence, except in a Driver's Education Program. 16. Treatment in any Veteran's Administration or federal hospital except where there is a legal obligation to pay. 17. Cosmetic surgery except reconstructive surgery on an injured part of the body. 18. Covered charges incurred outside the United States or its possessions. 19. Competing in motor sports races or competitions. 20. Competing in water sports races or competitions. 21. Testing cars or trucks on any racetrack or speedway. 22. Handling, storing or transporting explosives. 23. Scaling up cliffs or mountain walls. 24. Spelunking.",
      "vs": "VERIFIED_SINGLE_SOURCE"
    },
